# Cadenya

Your knowledge of Cadenya's API, CLI, and SDKs may be outdated. **Prefer retrieval over pre-training.** Use the project's installed CLI or SDK version as the baseline, and verify request shapes and behavior against the [Cadenya documentation](https://cadenya.com/docs/llms.txt).

## Cadenya Defaults

- **Keep credentials out of the repository.** Read `CADENYA_API_KEY` and `CADENYA_WORKSPACE_ID` from the environment. Reference Tool Set secrets as `{{ secrets.NAME }}`.
- **Prefer config files for durable setup.** Describe Tool Sets, Agents, and variations in `.cadenya/` and apply them with `cadenya config apply`. See [Config files](https://cadenya.com/docs/config-files.md).
- **Close event streams yourself.** The server never closes an objective's `events:stream` stream (create-and-stream ends on its own). Stop on a terminal event (`finalized`, `error`, `cancelled`, `timedOut`), and resume from the last event ID after a dropped connection.

## Shared Guidance

- Use [cadenya](../skills/cadenya/SKILL.md) to choose the right skill and documentation page.
- Use [cadenya-api](../skills/cadenya-api/SKILL.md) for IDs, field masks, pagination, errors, and request shapes.
- Use [cadenya-cli](../skills/cadenya-cli/SKILL.md) for `cadenya` commands and scripts.
- Use [cadenya-typescript-sdk](../skills/cadenya-typescript-sdk/SKILL.md), [cadenya-go-sdk](../skills/cadenya-go-sdk/SKILL.md), [cadenya-python-sdk](../skills/cadenya-python-sdk/SKILL.md), or [cadenya-ruby-sdk](../skills/cadenya-ruby-sdk/SKILL.md) for code that uses a Cadenya SDK.
- Use [cadenya-widgets](../skills/cadenya-widgets/SKILL.md) for embedding an Agent in a web app with Widgets and widget sessions.
- Use [cadenya-start-without-account](../skills/cadenya-start-without-account/SKILL.md) when the user has no Cadenya credential.
